From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] WindowManager: no rotation screenshot when the transition
 scale is 0

When the display rotates, WindowManager freezes it and covers it with a
screenshot, from which the rotation animation starts. SurfaceFlinger composes
that screenshot with GLES: on SwiftShader one capture took about 5 s of CPU
(PW3 Android, Test V48, screencap), so an app that asks for landscape froze
the device for several seconds on the way in and out. With a transition scale
of 0 nothing animates from the screenshot. The freeze itself stays (input is
held until the windows have redrawn); the rotation completes the way it does
on displays other than the default one, which never get a screenshot.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.java
@@ -6111,7 +6111,13 @@
         }
 
         // TODO(multidisplay): rotation on non-default displays
-        if (CUSTOM_SCREEN_ROTATION && displayContent.isDefaultDisplay) {
+        // PW3: with a transition scale of 0 there is no rotation animation to
+        // start from a screenshot, and taking it costs: SurfaceFlinger
+        // composes it with GLES, on SwiftShader about 5 s of CPU (PW3 Android,
+        // Test V48). The rotation then completes as on a display other than
+        // the default one, without a screenshot (stopFreezingDisplayLocked).
+        if (CUSTOM_SCREEN_ROTATION && displayContent.isDefaultDisplay
+                && getTransitionAnimationScaleLocked() != 0) {
             mExitAnimId = exitAnim;
             mEnterAnimId = enterAnim;
